A Clause is a disjunction of literals, basically a set of literals ( propositional formula or its negation ) 

A horn clause  is a clause with upto one positive literal

A definite horn clause has exactly one positive literal

Knowledge representation ;

A knowledge base is a finite set of rules
It’s a collection of clauses and formulas
It’s a set of formulas a1 … an which we consider all true

If B is a consequence of the KB then (a1 ^ … ^ am) → B is a tautology
K ⊨ φ  means K entails φ
φ is a consequence of K
K is a knowledge base and when the KB  is true φ must be true
K → φ is a tautology

Unit propagation is basic truth propagation where we can remove a existing fact from the body of other rules since we only need to consider possible contradiction, we can simply neglect anything forced to be true.

Fact extraction algorithm is where we input the KB and outputs its redux with all facts true given the KB K.

Unit resolutions is sound, it does not conclude something that is false.

Unit resolution is complete since it returns all the facts that are consequences of the KB

A fact is consequence of the KB K if it’s a fact in its redux. 
This means that K → K^ is a tautology

If particular K → x is a tautology, if x is a fact in K^

For complex entailments K ⊨ Y ← X1, … Xn we add the propositional variables in the body as facts to the existing KB and if its redux provides that Y is necessarily true then it does entail.

Computational complexity is where the worst case scenario in computing the redux of a KB is n*m where n rules and m variables and having all variables as facts.
A Knowledge base cannot express relationships between objects.

